{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity","id":1354031,"title":"PC Novas in Aeon Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-09T18:54:14-08:00","id":1354031,"title":"PC Novas in Aeon Trinity","content":"For the record, this is my take for my game. Others are perfectly free to alter, discard or ignore anything here for their own games. In deference to past custom with fam-made materials I will refer to book page numbers and otherwise be a little oblique to avoid copyright infringements.<br /> <br /> First, build the character as a human per the character creation rules outline in the Aeon Core pp. 34-38, though in this case Step 6 is eliminated. Note that the only two Nova-specific Edges are Attunement and Dormancy (Aberrant KS Manuscript Preview 2 pp 12-13). Eufiber is no longer a thing in Aeon.<br /> <br /> The Origin and Role Paths may be completed normal, but the Society Path needs a bit of clarification. For the most part the Society Paths of previous era have ceased to exist and it's unlikely (at best) that a Nova in the Aeon era would be taking most of the Psi Order Paths. Of the official Paths remain, some possibilities include the Freeland &quot;Psion&quot; (change &quot;psi powers&quot; to quantum powers), (replace Enhanced Attunement and Favored Mode with Attunement and Dormancy); The Nihonjin Agent (in addition to any other Cyberware, the Nova version of this guy gets a free, remotely activated Kill Switch (Aeon Aexpansion pp. 21). Another option might be as with Aeon Society Minerva Aeon pp 191, though you'll get a remote Kill Switch from them, too. A final option could be as part of the hidden Chitra Bhanu switching Attunement for Enhanced Attunement and Dormancy for Enhanced Psi Cloak. While these folks probably won't put an acid bomb in your brain, presumably pissing off S.K. Bhurano would have some deeply unpleasant consequences for your Nova character.<br /> <br /> After this apply a modified version of the Nova Template (Aberrant KS Manuscript Preview 2 pp 3-4) with the following changes: Along with a point of Quantum, they also receive a point of permanent Transcendence. They are still considered to be a Tier II character. Should they raise their Quantum to 6, they are considered to be a Tier III character at that point. While they can accept the Favored Attribute point, they may also choose to exchange it for an additional point of Quantum (along with a second point of Transcendence) and a point of either Attunement or Dormancy. Instead of a dot of Fame, they may choose a dot of Covert is that hasn't reach 2 dots yet. If both Covert and Alternate Identity are at 2 dots, the Nova may instead choose another Dot of Attunement, Dormancy or a dot chosen from one of his Paths).<br /> <br /> Instead of the normal XP, the nova gets 75 XP to spend on various abilities, at least 50 of which must be spent on Nova-specific traits (Quantum, Mega-Attributes, Attunement/Dormancy, etc) using the cost table (Aberrant KS Preview 2 pp. 4. Quantum may not be raised higher than 3 at this point. Quantum is also considered to be bought at half the normal cost, but each additional point of Quantum comes with an additional point of Transcendence (Should a character raise his Quantum to 4, they'll get 2 permanent points of Transcendence (1 for going to Quantum 4, the other for buying at half cost). Powers, Mega-Edges, Tags, etc can be found in Aberrant KS Preview 3 pp. 18-75. As usual, anyone (foolishly?) wishing to purchase a Quantum-based Trait (not including a Nova-specific Edges like Attunement or Dormancy) may do so at half the XP per Dot/Tag level, etc. For example, buying the &quot;Quantum Attack&quot; power with the &quot;Aggravated (2)&quot; Tag this way would give you 3 additional points of permanent Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Note that per changes in the Forums, the power tag &quot;Technique&quot; no longer exists. Instead, one may buy the Mega-Edge: Technique which otherwise obeys the rules and restrictions for Power Suites and Tags outlined at Aberrant KS Preview 3 pp 41-42.<br /> <br /> In addition to all of this, Aeon Nova apply a modified version of the &quot;Horror&quot; Tone at Aberrant KS Preview 3 pp 14. Along with what's listed there the Threshold for gaining Transformations (detailed in Aberrant KS Preview pp is 2 lower. So, along with their first, a Nova gains low-level transformations at Transcendence 2 and 3, Medium-level once at Transference 4 and 5 and high level ones for 6 and above. Note that they gain a Transformation for each dot of Transcendence they get. A nova with Transcendence 3 who buys Quantum 4 raises to Transcendence 5 and this gets two mid-level transformations.<br /> <br /> Reading through the above, it would be easy to assume that any Aeon Nova is doomed to swift, inevitable descent into becoming a twisted monstrosity. That is far from wrong. However, there is hope. Novas of this time period have potentially access to avenue that their previous counterparts did not with the advent of the Chitra Bhanu.<br /> <br /> In addition to the technique described for shedding temporary Flux in Aberrant KS Preview 2 pp. 7-8, a Nova may shed Flux more quickly with the help of a Quantakinetic. First, the nova must expend his Quantum down to 0. Then they must &quot;Dorm down per Dormancy (and thus have only normal human Health level) Next, a QK must use Drain on Aeon pp. 243. For these purposes, Corruption is effectively Quantum points. As this occurs, the Nova suffers injury (and pain) per Burning Out in Aberrant KS Preview 3 pp 20. Odd numbers of Quantum are rounded up to the next injury level (so a QK Draining 5 Quantum points would inflict Injury -1 damage on a fully healthy Nova. Finally, the Nova makes the Quantum+Composure with each success removing one Flux point for every two full Quantum points taking by the Drain with failure/botches having their usual effects. After all this, the Nova's Quantum template is something of a mess and he needs to heal his injuries with time, rest and medical care. Attempting to speed the healing with Psi or Quantum powers applies a +2 Complication for each injury level. Failure aggravates the injuries and causes the Nova to lose an additional injury level. A Botch aggravates the injury as above and also causes the Nova to gain temporary Flux equal to the higher of his Quantum or Permanent Transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 12-23-2019, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T04:48:06-08:00","id":1354111,"title":"","content":"I don't think there can be Nihonjin Agent Novas with the use of their anti-Inspired vaccine.<br /> Would this apply to Eden's Novas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T05:57:26-08:00","id":1354125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1354111#post1354111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there can be Nihonjin Agent Novas with the use of their anti-Inspired vaccine.<br /> Would this apply to Eden's Novas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd generally agree in terms of Nihonjin with the idea of the Nova agent being some kind of exception/experiment or something.<br /> <br /> Eden Novas would be rolled up in the normal way as Novas in the main Aberrant book (150 XP, Tier 3, etc) but with Origins, Roles and Society Paths unique to Eden.<br /> <br /> The above template is meant to roll up Novas from Earth and human colonies who did not descend into total Transcendence/Corruption at the moment of eruption.<br /> <br /> My take is that in the Aeon era true Nova eruption are very rare and occur when a baseline-latent is exposed to some source of Corruption/Quantum. Between the end of the Aberrant War and 2104 these eruption produced low-powered (Tier II, Quantum 1-3) Novas that were consumed with Transference and usually hunted down and killed though frequently with high casualties among the hunters. After 2104 and Bhuarno's noetic &quot;bomb,&quot; there was a chance for these Novas to emerge from their eruption with their sanity and humanity somewhat intact. But if they Hope to maintain their humanity, they'll have to be willing to Sacrifice for the good of others to build a Unity with the rest of the human race.<br /> <br /> In the Aberrant era Novas were rock stars, celebrities, modern day gods and goddesses (some of whom built literal cults that survive to this day). For Aeon Novas the watchwords are caution, restraint and temperance. Dormancy is almost a requirement for them and they'll tend to spend much of their time &quot;dormed down&quot; using their nova power only at times of great need or when they won't get caught. The Aeon Nova experience should be part X-Men (fighting for a world that fears and hates them) part <i>The Incredible Hulk</i> 80s TV show (Bill Bixby usually spend most of the show trying to deal with a situation until finally getting pushed too at which point a green-painted Lou Ferrigno smashes things and throws guys through plywood walls.<br /> <br /> While a party of Novas is possible, figure most of the time an Aeon Novas will end up as part of a group of Psions, Talents and others as someone able to deploy unique abilities that potentially have a terrible price. The Nova and his friends will need to keep his nature a secret - if not from other organizations then from the general public. At least until some suitably dramatic moment of revelation and, perhaps, acceptance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:51:12-08:00","id":1355258,"title":"","content":"You might want to check the unpbulished &quot;Asia Ascendent&quot; for 1E--the Nihonjin had a method to spark eruption in novas that they had determiend wouldn't be vulnerable to taint, which came with some fairly hefty rewstrictions (limited to Quantum 4 was the one I recall). I'd req","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:32:08-08:00","id":1355272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1355258#post1355258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to check the unpbulished &quot;Asia Ascendent&quot; for 1E--the Nihonjin had a method to spark eruption in novas that they had determiend wouldn't be vulnerable to taint, which came with some fairly hefty rewstrictions (limited to Quantum 4 was the one I recall). I'd req</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are &quot;Superiors,&quot; rules for which can be found in the \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T17:50:14-08:00","id":1355301,"title":"","content":"I like this. The idea of someone still trying to play hero reminds me of a dystopian Superman. Or just to be left alone a la The Hulk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:22:08-08:00","id":1355768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1355258#post1355258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to check the unpbulished &quot;Asia Ascendent&quot; for 1E--the Nihonjin had a method to spark eruption in novas that they had determiend wouldn't be vulnerable to taint, which came with some fairly hefty rewstrictions (limited to Quantum 4 was the one I recall). I'd req</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1355272#post1355272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those are &quot;Superiors,&quot; rules for which can be found in the \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asia Ascendant had rules for both Superiors and the &quot;Low-Taint&quot; Novas.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't want &quot;Low Taint/Flux/Transcendence&quot; Novas. Novas had their time in the sun during the Aberrant era and they collectively shit the bed. Those Novas from Nihonjin were essentially another iteration of the &quot;chosen few special ones&quot; here to save they day. That's not what I want for Aeon era Nova PCs.<br /> <br /> In 1944 a man who became known as William Stuart-Houston joined the United States Navy and received the Purple Heart after being wounded in battle. William Stuart-Houston's name during that time was William Hitler. Yeah, that Hitler. Adolph Hitler was this guy's half-uncle. Three of his sons are still alive today. The youngest one is 54. Imagine living that family history down.<br /> <br /> That's where PC Novas have to live. Many of them embrace their power and use it and fall to it. When the local legion smokes an Aberrant, often it's one of them. Still others ignore or deny their power, staying &quot;dormed down&quot; all the time denying their powers, pretending that they don't exist. PC Novas choose a third path, to try to use their abilities to help their world and the people in it without allowing their powers to consume them. It is a difficult, dangerous path, fraught with risks both internal and external. But then, that's kind of the point of being a PC, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 12-20-2019, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T00:22:00-08:00","id":1356012,"title":"","content":"That's effective. I will say that the current rules in Aberrant, which provide far fewer ways of reducing taint than 1E did suit that style of play--it's entirely too easy to get into a death spiral, and the moment you get a visible mutation or sign of taint, well--that's it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T04:42:22-08:00","id":1356040,"title":"","content":"One thing I'll include is a way to reduce Permanent Transcendence. In conjunction with a QK using Transference, a Nova needs to spend double the XP to buy a point of Quantum at the same level. Once that first, highest level of Transcendence has been removed, the Nova may continue to buy Transcendence down to a minimum of 1. So, if a Nova has Transcendence 6 to begin with, the Nova needs to drop 64 xp to reduce it to 5 and 32 more to reduce it to 4, etc. Obviously it's best to lose Transcendence before it gets higher than 5 and becomes entrenched.<br /> <br /> While Talents and Psions can fall back on their powers, Nova need to develop their &quot;human&quot; skills/attributes to be able to take of themselves without quickly falling back on their powers. Thus they can focus on shedding Flux quickly when it does occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T09:16:11-08:00","id":1356110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1355768#post1355768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Asia Ascendant had rules for both Superiors and the &amp;quot;Low-Taint&amp;quot; Novas.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't want &amp;quot;Low Taint/Flux/Transcendence&amp;quot; Novas. Novas had their time in the sun during the Aberrant era and they collectively shit the bed. Those Novas from Nihonjin were essentially another iteration of the &amp;quot;chosen few special ones&amp;quot; here to save they day. That's not what I want for Aeon era Nova PCs.<br /> <br /> In 1944 a man who became known as William Stuart-Houston joined the United States Navy and received the Purple Heart after being wounded in battle. William Stuart-Houston's name during that time was William Hitler. Yeah, that Hitler. Adolph Hitler was this guy's brother. Three of his sons are still alive today. The youngest one is 54. Imagine living that family history down.<br /> <br /> That's where PC Novas have to live. Many of them embrace their power and use it and fall to it. When the local legion smokes an Aberrant, often it's one of them. Still others ignore or deny their power, staying &amp;quot;dormed down&amp;quot; all the time denying their powers, pretending that they don't exist. PC Novas choose a third path, to try to use their abilities to help their world and the people in it without allowing their powers to consume them. It is a difficult, dangerous path, fraught with risks both internal and external. But then, that's kind of the point of being a PC, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Small correction. Willie Hitler was Adolf\u2019s nephew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T15:34:33-08:00","id":1356184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1356110#post1356110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Small correction. Willie Hitler was Adolf\u2019s nephew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, edited it in the post. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T08:57:06-08:00","id":1356652,"title":"","content":"Upon reflection, I've decided that these Aeon Novas remain Tier II unless they raise their Quantum to 6. Should they somehow reach Quantum 9 without getting to Transcendence 10 (there will be an XP expensive way to reduce permanent Transcendence), they become Tier IV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T15:47:24-08:00","id":1356708,"title":"","content":"Is there actually a point to being Tier IV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T15:58:29-08:00","id":1356713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1356708#post1356708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there actually a point to being Tier IV?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being really fuck-off powerful, I suppose. Presumably Tier IV will be covered in the Aberrant supplement: <i>Not Just Super-Powered, Super-Duper-Powered.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T22:02:37-08:00","id":1356755,"title":"","content":"Tiers seem to be used more in Scion than TC, where certain powers always work, don't work, or have a higher difficulty when differences of Tier are involved.<br /> <br /> It's also a good rule of thumb for how mich access to higher Scale they have through there powers. Tier 1 really doesn't, tier 2 has occasional access to scale, tier 3 has frequent access to scale, and tier 4 throws scale around all the time.<br /> <br /> For example, Proxies are Tier 3, and all of the proxy powers give additional scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T05:38:13-08:00","id":1356793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1356755#post1356755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tiers seem to be used more in Scion than TC, where certain powers always work, don't work, or have a higher difficulty when differences of Tier are involved.<br /> <br /> It's also a good rule of thumb for how mich access to higher Scale they have through there powers. Tier 1 really doesn't, tier 2 has occasional access to scale, tier 3 has frequent access to scale, and tier 4 throws scale around all the time.<br /> <br /> For example, Proxies are Tier 3, and all of the proxy powers give additional scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main difference I noted between Tiers 2 and 3 was the reduced success number. Getting successes on a 7 instead of an 8 makes a serious difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T15:44:07-08:00","id":1358493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1354111#post1354111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there can be Nihonjin Agent Novas with the use of their anti-Inspired vaccine.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that Nihonjin Agent Novas wouldn't work for other reasons, one important thing to note is that the Anti-Inspired vaccine actually fails to reach a fairly significant portion of Nippon's population: the &quot;forgotten people&quot; living in the &quot;unpopulated&quot; areas of the arcology. From the Aeon Corebook:<br /> <br /> The forgotten people living in the arcology\u2019s empty<br /> spaces are the government\u2019s biggest threat. They<br /> have difficulty leaving the arcology but haven\u2019t suffered<br /> the destruction of latency. The possibility of<br /> a nascent psionic population living in the forgotten<br /> parts of the city terrifies Nihonjin authorities.<br /> <br /> The thing is that anyone who is potentially psionicly latent is also potentially a Talent. Or a Nova.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":"to the last sentence 01-03-2020, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T18:47:03-08:00","id":1358517,"title":"","content":"And to be hoenst? Nihonjin might actually try to trigger a nova, espeically if they have a way to verity if taint is going to be an issue. Remember how much of their prosperity and safety was due to having non-tainted Novas, some of them mega-intelligent, serving the state.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T19:15:46-08:00","id":1358522,"title":"","content":"Given that Nippon had, until very recently, the world's only major concentration of Novas, it is also the only place outside a Corruption Zone even remotely likely for a new Nova to erupt. Given that they wouldn't know of the government's secret Novas, they'd have done everything possible to keep hidden for fear of being executed.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if everyone was tested for low-taint potential before they disappeared into 'uninhabited' arcology areas, they'd likely be a low-taint Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:50:11-08:00","id":1358536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358522#post1358522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Nippon had, until very recently, the world's only major concentration of Novas, it is also the only place outside a Corruption Zone even remotely likely for a new Nova to erupt. Given that they wouldn't know of the government's secret Novas, they'd have done everything possible to keep hidden for fear of being executed.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if everyone was tested for low-taint potential before they disappeared into 'uninhabited' arcology areas, they'd likely be a low-taint Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we know, there's no way to test for low flux/taint novas. Really there's no way to test for novas at all. There's a test that reveals that one can potentially be a Nova (or Psion/Psiad/Talent/Superior) but until that genetic die is &quot;rolled&quot; or they get dunked or made a Superior, there's no way to note what the person will become.<br /> <br /> Another point is that not everyone is tested. Figure if your background is that you're a loyal Nihonjin citizen living a normal life in the arcology, you can only become a Superior or a Talent because you'll be tested, noted and, assuming you pass the other tests of your loyalty/personality, undergo the Nakamura Process which either turns you into a Superior or &quot;fails&quot; and turns you into a Talent. The older generation of the &quot;disappeared&quot; mostly got tested and got the retrovirus, which stopped any chance of eruption, becoming a Psion/Psiad, or being a Talent. But the retrovirus doesn't necessarily eliminate genes for Quantum/Psi/Inspiration, it just prevents them from being expressed. Otherwise there wouldn't have been any Superiors because the genetic code for them would have long since been wiped out.<br /> <br /> The &quot;disappeared&quot; are having children. The percentage of them having children is generally higher than those living &quot;straight lives&quot; in the arcology. The children they have aren't being tested, except perhaps by the Akiyama group, which has limited resources at best. It's weird to think about, but in some ways the best place to start a group made up of Psiads, Superiors, Talents and Novas would be in the fringe areas of Nippon. Also, prior to closing itself off from the world, Nippon accepted millions of refugees, so character from Nippon, wouldn't necessarily have to be Japanese Asian in appearance or even have a Japanese name (though figure many of those refugees and their families would likely have done so to fit in better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 01-03-2020, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:51:38-08:00","id":1358537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358493#post1358493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that anyone who is psionicly latent is also potentially a Talent. Or a Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they\u2019re a latent they\u2019ve already headed down the psionic path and won\u2019t be Talent or nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T21:05:16-08:00","id":1358539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358537#post1358537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they\u2019re a latent they\u2019ve already headed down the psionic path and won\u2019t be Talent or nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>I edited my post to correct that. Even so the point remains that anyone who can become psionicly latent can also become a Nova or Talent depending on how the genetic die rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T21:57:57-08:00","id":1358545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358539#post1358539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I edited my post to correct that. Even so the point remains that anyone who can become psionicly latent can also become a Nova or Talent depending on how the genetic die rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. The genetics aren\u2019t precise - having the genetic markers doesn\u2019t make it guaranteed that you could or would move down a pathway towards psionic or quantum but it suggests it\u2019s a possibility. Talents are far less clear cut. Those same markers may point towards someone who\u2019ll become a Talent, but they may have nothing to do with another person who became a Talent who showed none of the markers when tested.<br /> <br /> Talents are always wild cards. You can\u2019t reliably predict them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T22:50:52-08:00","id":1358552,"title":"","content":"Unless someone smuggles in a Chamber the latents are kind of a moot point since they can't become psiads..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T03:59:28-08:00","id":1358582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358552#post1358552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless someone smuggles in a Chamber the latents are kind of a moot point since they can't become psiads..</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a chamber, being latent is not different from be the other kind of demi-powered (Aexpansion page 82), you have only half the potential.<br /> <br /> About the DNA mark, I view it as as dices rolling in the conception and not it the moment of eruption/learning/flux, but scientists can\u2019t say what\u2019s going to be until it happen. The virus can detect the 3 marks (Quantum, Psi and Inspiration) as they are the same, but a person born with the Psi mark would never become a Nova or Talent, they would slowly grow in Psi since early infancy until understand their powers. Same for a Nova, they had no chance of becoming a Psiad or Talent because when they were born the mark when to Quantum and the only natural way is to erupt.<br /> <br /> Superiors and Psions are different, they get the mark (no matter if it\u2019s pointing to Psi, Quantum or Inspiration) and turn it to the desired result (Psion or Superior). Psions are even better they pick half a mark (capacity of store energy) and turn into a full mark, pointed to Psi and activated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T21:53:13-08:00","id":1358999,"title":"","content":"I like to think that fully expressed Psiads fly under the Nihonjin's radar, so to speak, as maybe their tests only pickup on unexpressed markers, and then Psiads can hide their abilities, so you could have secret Psiads in the general populace of Nippon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T22:31:22-08:00","id":1359003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1358999#post1358999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think that fully expressed Psiads fly under the Nihonjin's radar, so to speak, as maybe their tests only pickup on unexpressed markers, and then Psiads can hide their abilities, so you could have secret Psiads in the general populace of Nippon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the general populace. Anyone &quot;on the grid&quot; in Nippon gets tested as a matter of course and someone with the genetic marker, including potential psiads, are noted and watched. Those interested in the wrong things, including/especially psionics, get the retrovirus, which ends any chance of being a psiad. Others undergo the Nakamura process and become either a Superior or a Talent.<br /> <br /> The only people in Nippon with a real chance to be Psiads are those within the population of the &quot;Forgotten.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T00:17:24-08:00","id":1359220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359003#post1359003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not the general populace. Anyone &amp;quot;on the grid&amp;quot; in Nippon gets tested as a matter of course and someone with the genetic marker, including potential psiads, are noted and watched. Those interested in the wrong things, including/especially psionics, get the retrovirus, which ends any chance of being a psiad. Others undergo the Nakamura process and become either a Superior or a Talent.<br /> <br /> The only people in Nippon with a real chance to be Psiads are those within the population of the &amp;quot;Forgotten.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was highlighting a potential grey area and or loophole that could open up character types and stories.<br /> <br /> It is not explicitly stated that they catch psiads, only latents, which are different.<br /> <br /> I was guessing at the expression of being a psiad is different from being a latent, kinda like how you don't have MR Coils until you're a nova. Which requires different tests to pick up on.<br /> <br /> If you are already psi active, I'm pretty sure kaga-2 doesn't take your abilities away, because Nippon having a way to neutralize Psions would be a big deal.<br /> <br /> It feels like it was a door that was left open, but not explicitly stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T08:30:09-08:00","id":1359293,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Psiads still have the correct genetic markers since the Psi Orders have accepted Psiads as valid subjects for their Prometheus Chambers, and the chambers can still identify those markers when changing a Psiad into a Psion. Successful use of Kaga-2 could possibly neutralize or weaken the powers of either type of psychic. OTOH the Doyen still have powers even though they lack bodies, and certain Telepathy and Electrokinesis powers can allow psychics to operate independently of their bodies.<br /> <br /> The Augendis Reinforce power would presumably make them resistant to the virus. Even if they lose their powers, the Iatrosis Adjust Template power would be able to undo the genetic changes. That does make me wonder if Adjust Template could be used to strip a Psion of their powers, since they're the result of genetic modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T10:13:42-08:00","id":1359314,"title":"","content":"Good point about Psiads testing for the orders, but then again the Prometheus chambers can't even force a Psiad to become a Psion.<br /> <br /> Again, I think it is open enough where a Psiad could slip through. I'm away from book, so I don't know if they bother with followup testing after the initial administration of the kaga-2, so they could just blindly trust it at this point, and not notice when it doesn't work on a psiad. And psiads can naturally mask their psi, so they could elude other detection methods. Or even if they do a test to see if it works, maybe it does seem to work initially, but your noetic template reinforces itself after the initial administration.<br /> <br /> If kaga-2 being a weapon against psions/psiads is cool for your table, then go for it. I think that secret psiads in Nippon is a cooler hook, but to each there own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T14:53:31-08:00","id":1359357,"title":"","content":"Latent and Psiads are different things, and a latent will not become a Psiad, but a Psiad will show to the genetic scan as a latent for a simple reason, latents are incomplete Psiads, they can store Psi but can\u2019t use them not even by training, while a Psiad will start showing some powers as soon as the psi trait raise to 2.<br /> <br /> Kaga-2 have no effect on already powered beings (Psiads, Psions, novas or superiors) as they already have developed what ever make them capable of using their power, it\u2019s not a potential genetic mark, but an organelle or noetic pattern that is properly established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T19:29:48-08:00","id":1359391,"title":"","content":"And yet a Psiad who steps into a Prometheus Chamber can have dots in modes outside their new Primary Aptitude stripped from them. Of course Prometheus Chambers are far more advanced than the Kaga-2 virus, and Psiads in Prometheus Chambers can still choose to reject the change. We do know for a fact that psionic beings who reject their abilities can remove them via genetic engineering, since the Coalition progenitors did this to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T02:32:21-08:00","id":1359432,"title":"","content":"The Psiad can do it ONLY if she want it, it\u2019s the intention behind that have this effect, as said in Aexpansion.<br /> <br /> Also, the Prometheus chamber is not only a genetic alteration machine, it is capable of change noetic patterns. If the genetic structure was the only thing affected, the Psions would get out of the chamber capable of learning powers, but they get out of the chamber capable of using the powers to a level Psiads can\u2019t (they can use the 5dot powers from the moment they are out, at a high difficulty and high cost, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T04:31:11-08:00","id":1359448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359220#post1359220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was highlighting a potential grey area and or loophole that could open up character types and stories.<br /> <br /> It is not explicitly stated that they catch psiads, only latents, which are different.<br /> <br /> I was guessing at the expression of being a psiad is different from being a latent, kinda like how you don't have MR Coils until you're a nova. Which requires different tests to pick up on.<br /> <br /> If you are already psi active, I'm pretty sure kaga-2 doesn't take your abilities away, because Nippon having a way to neutralize Psions would be a big deal.<br /> <br /> It feels like it was a door that was left open, but not explicitly stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can assume that Kaga-2 doesn't remove powers, it just prevents them from occurring if they haven't already. Figure that even after the &quot;lockdown&quot; in 2045 Nippon had a few agents out in the world and they tried this stuff on Novas - and it didn't work. Because if it had worked, they'd most likely have given it to the world to use against the Aberrants/Novas. Still, as long as a potential Novas hasn't fully erupted, Kaga-2 can neutralize their powers (AeEx notes that children showing &quot;signs of eruption&quot; are immediately given the retrovirus).<br /> <br /> I would still expect that Psaids from the main population of Nippon would be extremely rare. Psaids are very good at hiding their abilities from other powered beings like Novas and Psions. However, the Nihonjin aren't looking for Psaids, they're looking for potential Novas. So, any child manifesting weird headaches, strange visions, etc will likely be given the retrovirus to prevent &quot;eruption.&quot; There might well be a very few Psiads who somehow slipped through the net in the main population, but more than likely any Psiads or even Novas in Nippon will be among the population of the Forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T04:35:25-08:00","id":1359449,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s best to assume that we\u2019re probably not going to lock this down one way or the other (no meta plot, remember), but let groups use whichever works for them and have the story potential flow from both possibilities across the Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T09:23:31-08:00","id":1359506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359432#post1359432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Psiad can do it ONLY if she want it, it\u2019s the intention behind that have this effect, as said in Aexpansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely true, as I expressly noted in my post:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Psiads in Prometheus Chambers can still choose to reject the change. </div> </div> </div>You're apparently trying to somehow prove me wrong by agreeing with what I actually said.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359432#post1359432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Prometheus chamber is not only a genetic alteration machine, it is capable of change noetic patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also true, as I implied in my post:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course Prometheus Chambers are far more advanced than the Kaga-2 virus... </div> </div> </div>So you're once more trying to argue against statements I never actually made. It seems to me you read the very first sentence of my post, then scrawled out a reply screed without bothering to read the remaining two sentences, which would have countered your arguments. I will state right now that, no matter what you write, I will never, ever believe that you cannot remove noetic powers via gene editing since, as I noted in my post's third and final sentence, it is Trinity Continuum canon that it can be done:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We do know for a fact that psionic beings who reject their abilities can remove them via genetic engineering, since the Coalition progenitors did this to themselves. </div> </div> </div>To further expand on that point, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, page 362:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the final transformation from individual progenitors to a telepathic group mind required several years and, during this time, a few members of this species viewed the coming transformation with horror and alarm. Not wishing to lose their individuality, they used genetic surgery to remove their own psionic gifts and fled from the rest of their species in six vast space arks. </div> </div> </div>So a group of beings with psionic gifts rejected their psionic gifts and used genetic surgery to remove their psionic gifts, ergo it is possible - at least under certain circumstances - for gene editing to remove active noetic powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T12:42:01-08:00","id":1359549,"title":"","content":"If tier 2 Nova's still exist on Earth there would probably be some sort of secret society that might support them. Might be interesting to let the players design such a society from scratch. Also Aeon Trinity might themselves be protecting some of them, which would allow the player access to that Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T14:19:11-08:00","id":1359571,"title":"","content":"Not contradicting you, agreeing with you and reforcing the points. Maybe it was kind of useless post...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 01-07-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T14:27:58-08:00","id":1359573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359549#post1359549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If tier 2 Nova's still exist on Earth there would probably be some sort of secret society that might support them. Might be interesting to let the players design such a society from scratch. Also Aeon Trinity might themselves be protecting some of them, which would allow the player access to that Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no tier 2, Novas, all novas are Tier 3 or 4, that\u2019s basically what define them as Novas. A \u201ctier 2 Nova\u201d would be much like a natural Superior or a Stalwart, as far as we know, as apparently the capacity of use quantum on effects beyond your own body require a Tier 3 quantum power.<br /> <br /> I believe those Stalwarts exist in Earth and would not be detected as Nova by any mean except a very sophisticated quantum detector (like a quantakinetic, a nova or an good powered super Science item based on them).<br /> <br /> Your idea for a secret society is awesome, I think project Cetos would be the ones studding them in Aeon Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T14:33:06-08:00","id":1359574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359573#post1359573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no tier 2, Novas, all novas are Tier 3 or 4, that\u2019s basically what define them as Novas. A \u201ctier 2 Nova\u201d would be much like a natural Superior or a Stalwart, as far as we know, as apparently the capacity of use quantum on effects beyond your own body require a Tier 3 quantum power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not read the first post? The whole proposition of this thread is about creating Tier 2 Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T16:48:05-08:00","id":1359604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359574#post1359574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you not read the first post? The whole proposition of this thread is about creating Tier 2 Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is about making Novas in the Aeon era, with the OP providing their own house rules for Nova creation which reduces them to tier 2. Since the OP defines a Tier 2 Nova as one who hasn't yet hit Quantum 6, I'd say there are likely some scattered about. Trinity Continuum: Aeon, page 332 gives quick rules for Aberrants which include Tier 2 'Divergent' class Aberrants, who are described as being &quot;young or weak&quot;. I figure that means Quantum 1 to 3, with well under the standard 150 xp of a starting character. If the Corruption score is equal to quantum, then all but Terat class Aberrants (Corruption 6-8) count as Tier 2 for the OP's homebrew system.<br /> <br /> Trinity Continuum: Aeon, page 365 indicates there are hostile Aberrants left on Earth. Several of unknown power were hiding in Wycoff's Blight. Two powerful Aberrants (Janos and Janice Karagian?) were in the Olympus Underworld, and several aquatic Aberrants of undefined power level were following Felice Taylor. The book covers an Aberrant cult lead by an Aberrant named Whispernet on pages 339-340, although I'm uncertain if their quantum is above 5 (if Corruption=Quantum, they're only Quantum 4). There could easily have been more Aberrants, or even uncorrupted Novas, around the world who didn't join in on the attack.<br /> <br /> As for whether any of them besides Whispernet have followers, the ones from Wycoff's Blight likely have aberrant cults of their own. Felice was likely too crazy, and her followers were possibly too close to her to get followers of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":".  spelling corrections 01-08-2020, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T17:27:05-08:00","id":1359608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359604#post1359604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thread is about making Novas in the Aeon era, with the OP providing their own house rules for Nova creation which reduces them to tier 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused, isn't that basically what I just said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T21:53:48-08:00","id":1359646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359608#post1359608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused, isn't that basically what I just said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was clarifying why Mateus would claim there are no Tier 2 Novas while also responding to Jeremy's statement regarding both the likelihood of Tier 2 Novas on Earth, and the possibility of them having secret allies; which required trying to convert Aeon text to OP homebrew.<br /> <br /> Mateus is correct in that the Aberrant manuscript starts all Novas (even at Quantum 1) at Tier 3.<br /> <br /> The Aeon book's condensed Aberrant rules provides weak adversary Novas (Corruption 2-3) who're Tier 2.<br /> <br /> The OP posited an alternate set of rules in which all pre-Quantum 6 Novas are Tier 2.<br /> <br /> That clarification was needed so I could answer the earlier question regarding the likelihood of Tier 2's being around and having secret support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:52:21-08:00","id":1359654,"title":"","content":"Warning: I haven't read the thread yet; so my comments may be out of whack. <br /> <br /> I see there being two basis strains of eximorphs: the Enhanced, of which Superiors are a Tier 2 example and Dark Stars are a Tier 3 example; and the Empowered, of which Novas are the Tier 3 example. The distinction is that the Enhanced are limited to Mega-Edges and (at Tier 3) Mega-Attributes, while the Empowered also have access to Quantum Powers.<br /> <br /> Now, Superiors don't actually have access to Mega-Edges; what they have are lower-powered conceptual counterparts (the Superior powers). But they <i>are</i> conceptual counterparts: both are built around the premise that they enhance the character's existing abilities in some way: they're directed inward. From here on, I'll use \u201cAugmentation\u201d to refer to any inward-focused power, whether it's a Superior Power, a Mega-Edge, or a Mega-Attribute. By contrast, Quantum Powers are about affecting the world around the Empowered; they're directed outward. And the powers that Tier 2 Empowered have access to that Tier 2 Enhanced don't should likewise be directed outward. <br /> <br /> At Tier 2, I'd consider the possibility of saying that you're either Enhanced or Empowered, but not both; this would be in contrast to Novas being both. On the other hand, an argument could be made that Augmentations are the birthright of all eximorphs, and that Tier 2 Empowered ought to have access to both: in particular, the biggest difference between eximorphs and psychomorphs is that the former has access to Augmentations while everything that the latter gets is more akin to Quantum Powers. <br /> <br /> Either way, the superhuman abilities that the Tier 2 Empowered have that the Enhanced don't should arguably be patterned loosely off of Psion Aptitudes \u2014 not in terms of how they're organized (I'm <i>not</i> saying \u201ceight Aptitudes with three Modes of chains of five powers each\u201d), but rather in terms of how much a Tier 2 Empowered's powers ought to be able to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T00:37:05-08:00","id":1359662,"title":"","content":"Tier 2 Powers should have scale locked in 1 or 2, 3 at maximum, so the difference between them is never overwhelming, like the Psion Powers. Saying that, a Q2 Nova could be Tier 2, enhanced or empowered.<br /> <br /> The point is, Tier 2 \u201csuperhumans\u201d are limited to Enhancements and not Powers per se, that\u2019s basically what we see in Superiors and Stalwarts. So a tier 2 Nova should work around that idea.<br /> <br /> If you want a tier 2 \u201cempowered\u201d that\u2019s ok, and the idea of making their powers similar to Psions powers is a great option, but my point would be Tier 2 Novas are limited to mega attributes and mega edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T14:08:38-08:00","id":1359773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1359662#post1359662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tier 2 Powers should have scale locked in 1 or 2, 3 at maximum, so the difference between them is never overwhelming, like the Psion Powers. Saying that, a Q2 Nova could be Tier 2, enhanced or empowered.<br /> <br /> The point is, Tier 2 \u201csuperhumans\u201d are limited to Enhancements and not Powers per se, that\u2019s basically what we see in Superiors and Stalwarts. So a tier 2 Nova should work around that idea.<br /> <br /> If you want a tier 2 \u201cempowered\u201d that\u2019s ok, and the idea of making their powers similar to Psions powers is a great option, but my point would be Tier 2 Novas are limited to mega attributes and mega edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those good points, though I'll flip it around a bit. Tier II PC Aeon Novas don't get Mega-Attributes and the Mega-Edges keyed off of them - at least not until they achieve Quantum 6 and become Tier 3. Now, they can purchase Mega-Edges keyed off of Quantum itself, since that how Novas simulate &quot;Power Suites&quot; like Weather Control, etc. Tier II Novas may purchase certain Mega-Edges as Techniques of a power, but cannot get Mega-Attributes/Mega-Edges until they reach Quantum 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T16:36:39-08:00","id":1360224,"title":"","content":"Raises the question. Should Superiors be able to buy mega edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T17:08:58-08:00","id":1360230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1360224#post1360224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raises the question. Should Superiors be able to buy mega edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no. Now, they might be able to buy stuff that's similar to some Mega-Edges (cyberware that gives them the ability to see in the dark ala Mega-Vision) but they can't buy actual Mega-Vision because they aren't Novas.<br /> <br /> And in terms of PC Novas, their ability to buy certain Mega-Edges is limited. One with Elemental Mastery (Time) might be able to obtain the Mega-Edges, Fast Worker or Mega-Speed as Techniques, but those are limited by their base Quantum score. Assuming they could find (or make) it, they could possible gain Mega-Attributes or Mega-Edge via Q-Tech. But in Aeon, Q-Tech is going to be very, very rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 01-10-2020, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T17:51:04-08:00","id":1360241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1360224#post1360224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raises the question. Should Superiors be able to buy mega edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>johntfs resumes my view.<br /> <br /> But I need to add a small detail: Most of the Superior powers are kind of weak versions of MEdgs or MAttributes. Let\u2019s say Speedster requires 3 dots to grant 2 scales in speed, while mega speed requires less, and can reach much further in speed scale. So in a way, the Superiors are gaining Medges, just calling it different names...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T18:10:02-08:00","id":1360248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mostlyjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1360224#post1360224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raises the question. Should Superiors be able to buy mega edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly not, IMO. You could adapt some mega-edges to have Superior power versions but they wouldn\u2019t be mega-edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T18:50:07-08:00","id":1360257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1354031-pc-novas-in-aeon-trinity?p=1360241#post1360241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> johntfs resumes my view.<br /> <br /> But I need to add a small detail: Most of the Superior powers are kind of weak versions of MEdgs or MAttributes. Let\u2019s say Speedster requires 3 dots to grant 2 scales in speed, while mega speed requires less, and can reach much further in speed scale. So in a way, the Superiors are gaining Medges, just calling it different names...</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to consider is that there are a lot of paths to the same result. One of the possible &quot;Super-science&quot; items mentioned in Trinity Core is a Freeze Ray. A Talent could make some kind of gun that fires liquid Helium. A Psion could use Thermakinesis. A Nova could use Quantum Bolt. Generally if you look hard enough, you can find something in your character's abilities that will let you do something similar to what others can do without doing exactly what they do - or at least exactly how they do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T15:02:09-08:00","id":1360766,"title":"","content":"I do hope we get to habe more Superior powers one day. ... Actually, that makes me look forward to Adventure as Stalwarts and Mesmerists had cool powers in 1e, a fact I expect to continue in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}